{"primary": "SORT", "secondary": "PAR", "subform": "sign/width obligation (uint-to-int conversion wraps negative, bypasses bounds check)", "justification": "The obligation is over one carrier, the DiscReason value decoded from the discMsg RLP payload, and one edge, its String()/log formatting site. The pre-fix code decodes it as an unbounded uint, so it is not constrained to the one-byte reason sort. The witness is a crafted discMsg whose reason is huge, for example at least 2^63. Converting it to int wraps negative, so it passes the less-than-length bounds check, and the table index then panics when high-verbosity logging formats the reason. The fix narrows the carrier to uint8. A single-site sign/width violation is the most local basis, so SORT wins on both count and tie order. PAR applies only secondarily: the lenient decoder accepts payloads that a peer encoder of a valid DiscReason would never produce."}
```

