{"primary": "SORT", "secondary": "PAR", "subform": "absent/nil member of an option-like result read as present (nil dereference at one site)", "justification": "The obligation is over a single site in the GetTrieNodes handler and one in trie.tryGetNode. At that site a value that can be the 'absent' member is read as the 'present' member: snap.Account returns nil with no error for a non-existent account, and the handler then reads account.Root. Likewise, tryGetNode reaches a nil origNode at the end of the path and treats it as a real node. The witness is a malicious GetTrieNodes request whose path set names a non-existent account, or a path that ends on an empty subtrie, which makes the node crash on a nil dereference. A PAR reading also fits, because tryGetNode's nil handling differs between the descend branch and the end-of-path branch. But PAR names two paths and the edge between them, whereas SORT names only the one site, so SORT is minimal and comes first in the tie order."}
```

